# Watchlist for ble-fingerprint.py
#
#   ./scripts/ble-fingerprint.py --input logs/capture.log \
#       --watchlist config/watchlist.conf
#
# One matcher per line. Text after '#' becomes the note shown on a hit.
#
# Matchers:
#   AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF   an observed address
#   name:<substring>    matches the advertised name, case-insensitive
#   <serial>            a serial extracted from an advertised name
#   <fingerprint>       the 12-character content fingerprint, or a full
#                       identity key such as 'addr:...' or 'serial:...'
#
# Which matcher to use depends on how the device advertises. Run the tool once
# without a watchlist and read the KEY and TIER columns first:
#
#   strong     public address, or a serial in the name. Safe to watch by
#              address or serial; it identifies one unit.
#   session    random static address. Safe to watch by address for as long as
#              the device stays powered, but it changes after a reboot.
#   model      the address rotates, so only the fingerprint persists, and it
#              identifies a product rather than a unit. Several people with the
#              same headphones share one fingerprint.
#   ambiguous  not enough distinguishing content to attribute to anything.
#              Watching these produces hits that mean nothing.
#
# Watching a 'model' or 'ambiguous' entry is a lead, not an identification.

# --- examples, delete these -------------------------------------------------
# name:flipper            # Flipper Zero default advertised name
# name:marauder           # ESP32 Marauder
# DA:AB:97:C5:53:68       # device seen loitering, logged 2026-08-04
